E. References (read for behaviour and interfaces; no code copied)
   - Linux mac80211 and cfg80211 (net/mac80211, net/wireless), the Linux
     kernel headers, and btrtl (drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c): the mac layer
     (mac/), the Linux API layer (compat/) and the Bluetooth patch loader
     (bt/) are new implementations. compat/ provides Linux kernel interfaces
     (names, structure layouts, macro and function signatures) because the
     unmodified rtw89 sources are compiled against them.
     bt/rtkbtfw/epatch.c contains the project-id to LMP-subversion table and
     the patch-file rules of btrtl.c as interoperability facts.
   - Microsoft Windows-driver-samples (network/wlan/wificx, network/wlan/WDI,
     network/netadaptercx; MS-PL): the WiFiCx front end (wificx/) follows the
     structure of the WiFiCx sample. No sample code is included.
   - Test vectors in driver/crypto.c: RFC 4493 (AES-CMAC) and
     IEEE Std 802.11-2020 Annex J.6.4 (CCMP).

